      "id": "3a2b797d2067c37742fc54d33d8d558dce1b6cc0",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 693324786,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Note that if this returns an EOF indication - returns FALSE and `*err` is 0 - it should set `*err` to `WTAP_ERR_SHORT_READ`, because, while you might get an EOF indication on a *sequential* read, you should never get it on a *random-access* read, as you presumably successfully read the packet the first time.\n\n(Note also that we could do this at the topmost libwiretap level, so that it applies for C and Lua file readers.)",
